    "lawCode": "Add §131-aaa, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4322\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to landlords of\nhousing accommodations occupied by recipients of public assistance\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nRelates to landlords of housing accommodations occupied by recipients\nof public assistance.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThe social services law is amended by adding a new section 131-aaa.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis bill would require that the owner of a building containing the\nhousing accommodations into which the recipient of public assistance\nand care intends to move shall file with the local department of\nsocial services a verified statement that the building containing the\nhousing accommodations meets all applicable building codes,\nordinances, and regulations of the municipality where the building is\nlocated. The local social services department would be authorized to\nwithhold public assistance payments to a landlord or to any other\nperson for or toward the rental of any housing accommodations occupied\nby public assistance recipients. The verified statement would have to\nbe filed prior to any payment being made by or on behalf of the local\ndepartment of social services. A statement would have to be filed\nevery 6 months.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007-08, A.1511; Held for Consideration in Social Services 2005-06,\nA.8216; Held for Consideration in Social Services\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
